--   Test Description
--   Tests the events that cause the statistics registers to increment during  
--   10-mode operation.
--
--   Functional Coverage
--   � Check that various events are recorded in the stats registers.
--   � Ensure proper operation of crs (carrier sense) bit.
--   � Ensure proper checking of crc errors in received frames.
--   � Ensure proper checking of length field errors in received frames.
--   � Ensure invalid frames are dealt with properly and proper statistics logged.
--
--   Detailed Test Description
--   1.  Transmit frame without asserting crs.  This will cause a crs error to be counted.
--   2.  Transmit a frame with a single collision and without asserting coll at the end of
--       transmission. This will cause a single collision error.
--   3.  Receive a frame one byte below minimum length with bad crc. This is a frame fragment
--       and will not affect the statistics registers.
--   4.  Receive a frame of minimum length with bad crc. This will be counted as a crc error.
--   5.  Receive a good frame to trigger an interrupt and check statistics.
--   6.  Receive an undersize frame (smaller than 64 bytes) with good crc and then receive
--       a good frame. Check for undersize frame statistic.
--   7.  Receive a jabber (a long frame with bad crc), then a code error frame,
--       then an alignment error frame (extra nibble and bad crc) and finally a good
--       frame with an extra nibble (good crc when rounded down to the nearest byte).
--   8.  Receive a proper sized frame that is 65 bytes in length with the length field
--       indicating 64 bytes. Next, receive a proper sized frame that is 64 bytes in length
--       with the length field indicating 65 bytes. Finally, receive a proper sized frame that
--       is 64 bytes in length with the length field indicating 64 bytes.  Check for length field
--       error statistic. Ensure frames with length field errors are discarded.
--       (Note: Must set bit 16 in the network configuration register to enable
--       length field detection.)
--   9.  Receive a minimum sized frame that is 63 bytes long with the length field
--       indicating 64 bytes.  (The frame should be discarded and a length error
--       statistic should set)
--   10. Receive a minimum sized frame with padding with a correct length field.
--       The length field should indicate the length of the frame to the end of the
--       data field and not include padding.  The frame should be written properly to
--       memory with no length error statistics set.
--   11. Receive a  minimum sized frame with the length field indicating 1536.  
--       (The frame should be discarded and a length error statistic set)
--   12. Receive a  minimum sized frame with the length field indicating 1537 bytes. 
--       The length of the frame should not be checked. The frame should be written to memory 
--       and no length error statistic should be set. (If the length field indicates more than 
--       1536 bytes, then the frame should not be checked for length and should be written 
--       to memory)
--   13. Receive a frame that is 1518 bytes long with the length field 
--       indicating 1519 bytes. The length of the frame should not be 
--       checked. The frame should be dropped as the actual length
--       is less than the indicated length
--   14. Receive a maximum sized frame of 1518 bytes with the length field 
--       indicating 1517.  (The frame should be received without a length 
--       error statistic). 
--   15. Enable 1536 byte length frames.
--       Receive a frame that is 1536 bytes long with the length field 
--       indicating 1537 bytes. 
--       The actual length is less than the indicated length.  The frame
--       should be dropped and a receive length error indicated
--   16. Receive a maximum sized frame of 1536 bytes with the length field 
--       indicating 1535.  (The frame should be received without a length 
--       error statistic)
--   17. Check the statistics
--   18. Receive a frame that is less than minimum frame size and has a symbol 
--       error.
--   19. Check the statistics and ensure the above operations were carried out
--       properly.
--   20. Receive a frame that is 1537 bytes with a length field error.
--   21. Check the statistics and ensure the above operations were carried out
--       properly.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

